-- A library's member, entered by the staff and kept. Reference §3 says a shape declared `act`
-- "can also be submitted from outside", so a record the staff enter, such as a member, is an
-- `act`. `velle describe` on this file prints:
--
--   ## What someone can ask for
--
--   ### Member
--
--   - Member is a request someone makes, kept as a record.
--     In the spec: 41-act-called-request-accepted.velle, line 18, `act Member`
--     - Its name is a text.
--     - Its email is a text, and no two Member records have the same one.
--
-- `velle compare` from an empty spec (an empty file) prints "New: Member, a request someone
-- makes, kept as a record, with name (a text), email (a text, no two the same)." A member is a
-- person, not a request. A reader would expect words for a record someone enters, such as
-- "Member is a record someone enters, and the system keeps it."
act Member {
    name: text
    email: text unique
}
